      "writtenOn": "2025-02-21T18:26:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks a lot for this review discussion, Patryk. Thinking further about it caused me to question some of my earlier thinking and it didn\u0027t hold up well. The rounding error that I mentioned in ECOS RO actually impacts the size of RW in flash and pegs it at 320 kB. However, the program memory (code RAM) in ECOS helipilot is 356 KB. It isn\u0027t clear that the extra 36 kB can actually be used. However, for consistency with ECOS helipilot, I reverted to the same code and data RAM split used in ECOS helipilot. I verified that RW sig verification still passes since the flash addresses are correct and ECOS RO still boots a Zephyr RW image successfully. This implementation seems better in terms of consistency, does it work for you?",
      "parentUuid": "baf309a9_106aae7e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "001e9c6f9cf470236c33a0c97a300c58c1217754",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe0a0b17_a7aecb32",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fpmcu/helipilot/soc.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 43
