      "message": "\u003e I think so, but now that the code/data split is consistent with ECOS helipilot\n\nNot really. Now we tell zephyr that it has 352kB for code.\n\nSince the 352/156 split was the initial choice for helipilot, I would leave the split here and override it once again in `helipilot.dts`.\n\nI would also change the `Update program/data memory size` comments to the following\n\n```\n           ┌──────────────┐           \n           │   Reserved   │           \n           │     4KB      │           \n           ├──────────────┤0x200D7000 \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │   Data RAM   │           \n           │     156KB    │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n 0x100B0000├──────────────┤0x200B0000 \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │   Code RAM   │           \n           │     352KB    │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n           │              │           \n 0x10058000└──────────────┘           \n\n```",
